{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1112744-veneficti-or-the-cirlce-of-red-sources-needed","id":1112744,"title":"Veneficti or the Cirlce of Red, Sources needed.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-07T09:42:32-07:00","id":1112744,"title":"Veneficti or the Cirlce of Red, Sources needed.","content":"I have been searching for a book containing the pillars and other rules regarding the Circle of Red, I've managed to grind myself into madness trying to find these buggers in the title. I was wondering if anyone in here could let me know in which book it is they're found so I can finally finish my prep for a Dark Ages vampire campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5612-shadeworld","name":"Shadeworld","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:52:18-07:00","id":1112751,"title":"","content":"Dark Ages: Devil's Due.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:52:27-07:00","id":1112752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeworld</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1112744-veneficti-or-the-cirlce-of-red-sources-needed#post1112744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been searching for a book containing the pillars and other rules regarding the Circle of Red, I've managed to grind myself into madness trying to find these buggers in the title. I was wondering if anyone in here could let me know in which book it is they're found so I can finally finish my prep for a Dark Ages vampire campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only reference to the &quot;Circle Of Red&quot; that I can spontaneously find is in the 'Mage Storyteller's Handbook', page 198.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Older Vampire supplements vaguely mentioned<br /> a mage order called the Circle of Red, for example.<br /> Hints suggested that the Circle might be somehow<br /> related to House Tytalus of the Order, and other<br /> phrases suggested that the Tzimisce vampires had<br /> unholy connections with certain Tytalus mages.<br /> Clever Storytellers might see the shared interests of<br /> Koldunic sorcerers and Circle mages. </div> </div> </div>The Circle of Red seems to be a Vampire-books only thing, there is no reference in the Mage books. But you might want to read up on House Tytalus itself, as it is described in the modern Order Of Hermes Tradition splatbooks. Alternatively, the &quot;Dark Ages: Mage Grimoire&quot; book seems to describe that house, maybe in a more timeline-fitting way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-07-2017, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:55:58-07:00","id":1112756,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot you two, Marin hit it on the nose. <br /> <br /> I will definitely look up Tytalus, Ambrosia.. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5612-shadeworld","name":"Shadeworld","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T11:53:05-07:00","id":1116496,"title":"","content":"Tytalus is pretty interesting in Ars Magica, which it was ported over from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":